 an empire, makes political decisions as an aspiring emperor and positions armies; battles then play out in real time on land, sea and air. During those fights the ruler can take dragon form to join the action personally and support the troops.\n\nThe result blends governing, role-playing and real-time tactics. Larian Studios developed it, and it includes both single-player and multiplayer. It suits strategy players who want a mix of governance, tactics and direct action rather than a single narrow RTS loop."}}